# Compact and semantically colored desktop logs
Workstream-ID: lea-18
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/18
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed desktop console implementation and fictional offline fixtures
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make narrow run-console output readable without losing diagnostics
Dependencies: lea-11

## Purpose
Replace oversized diagnostic prefixes in the desktop console with compact
time, severity and activity labels. Preserve full output through a diagnostic
view, the existing file logs and unchanged CLI execution behavior.
Use semantic theme colors and natural wrapping rather than color alone.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace current console rendering, source metadata, themes and process streaming.
- [x] Implement compact severity/activity labels and original-prefix viewing.
- [x] Preserve prompts, multiline diagnostics, theme repainting and bounded history.
- [x] Verify focused regressions and narrow dark/light layouts with fictional data.
- [x] Update directly affected guides and reviewed demonstration media.
- [x] Verify the scoped issue, Project identity and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Ordinary log records show compact time, level and appropriate activity labels.
- [x] Success, caution and failure use distinct semantic colors in both themes.
- [x] Messages wrap at spaces; long tokens remain readable without horizontal overflow.
- [x] Diagnostic prefixes remain available without restarting or changing log levels.
- [x] Prompts and multiline/unknown output are not dropped or interpreted as markup.
- [x] Theme changes recolor the backlog and do not duplicate partial output.
- [x] Existing settings, unrelated dirty work and published releases are preserved.
- [x] Offline verification is not represented as a live application or human approval.

## Completion evidence
Locally implemented plain-text formatted spans, compact time/severity/activity
badges, original-source tooltips and reversible Details. Unknown output,
literal markup, indentation, streaming prompts and split ANSI/CRLF sequences
are preserved. The bounded backlog repaints in either theme; appending does
not steal the reader's selection or scroll position.

GUI notices distinguish configuration, input, commands and errors. A process
ending successfully is DONE, cancellation is STOPPED and failure is ERROR;
none is presented as proof of application submission. Submission attempt,
confirmed submission and dry-run activity retain separate meanings.

The five focused GUI suites passed all 145 tests with native process exit
zero. Scoped Ruff/Black checks passed for the six changed Python files;
GUI mypy passed for nine source files. Independent 360-pixel dark/light
console checks confirm no horizontal overflow and reversible original text.
Direct sampled visual review covers expanded dark Run, compact light Run
and a paired narrow-theme console sheet, not complete animation playback
or human aesthetic acceptance.

Affected guides and fictional source previews are refreshed. The run GIF
has nine frames, a 17.8-second loop and 1026086 bytes; the tutorial GIF is
unchanged. All twenty-four retained README relative references resolve.
Original selected private size/mtime metadata and native preferences match
their baseline; HEAD is unchanged and the index has no staged changes.
Prior README curation and unrelated work are retained.

This is source-only offline completion. Full file/CLI logging and child
execution are unchanged. No live run, commit, push, package build, release
replacement or human acceptance is included. Scoped completion settlement
is recorded separately in the navigation index and development ledger.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-09: Completed compact, naturally wrapped, semantically colored
  desktop logs and reversible diagnostics. Focused integration, isolated
  native presentation, documentation and preservation checks passed.
  Keep the existing distributed executable and live-qualification boundaries.
- 2026-11-09: Started bounded desktop-log improvements. The existing renderer
  makes spaces nonbreaking and retains long source prefixes in the compact
  console. Preserve original diagnostics and use only fictional public examples.
